.\" Educational secure-coding reference. Generated, not hand-edited.
.TH CWE-502 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-502 \- Deserialization of Untrusted Data
.SH RANK
2025 CWE Top 25 rank: \fB#15\fR (2024 rank: 16).
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: Injection / Data Handling.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Untrusted data is deserialized without sufficient verification. Rich formats can reconstruct arbitrary object graphs and trigger callbacks during construction, so a crafted payload ('gadget chain') can lead to remote code execution, denial of service or logic tampering.
.SH MITIGATION
Do not deserialize untrusted data with formats that can execute code (pickle, Java native serialization, PHP unserialize, node\-serialize). Use a data\-only format such as JSON, validate against a schema, and if unavoidable restrict allowed types and sign the payload.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB71\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
